       "old": "pairs (q,t0) with q a point of I+ and t0 in [0,T) such that the tail gamma([t0,T)) is contained in the causal past J^-(q) intersected with M. Whole-curve containment gamma([0,T)) subset J^-(q) is strictly STRONGER and is NOT the predicate of this class [rev12: F1-review-19 HF-06 critical, independently confirmed by worker-037 W037V2-F1 and worker-078 W078-F1-QUANT-ADJ-01]",
       "new": "pairs (q,t0) with q a point of I+ and t0 in [0,T) such that the tail gamma([t0,T)) is contained in the causal past J^-(q) intersected with M. Whole-curve containment gamma([0,T)) subset J^-(q) is EQUIVALENT to the tail form for causal geodesics, because J^-(q) is past-closed (for t < t0, gamma(t) <= gamma(t0) <= q), so the tail formulation is a definitional choice and NOT a weakening; neither reading is a second predicate of this class. [rev13: strict-order direction corrected - W076-GFORM-STRICTNESS-RECONCILE-06 T1 (0/355 preorders on 4 points separate the readings) and worker-040 W040-F1-STRICTNESS-ADJ-04; the rev12 'strictly STRONGER' assertion was false]",
